  "raw_text": "Step 1: Since $AB$ is the diameter of the circle, $\\angle ACB$ is a right angle (90°) because any angle inscribed in a semicircle is a right angle.\n\nStep 2: The sum of the angles in a triangle is 180°. Therefore, for $\\triangle ABC$, we have:\n\\[\n\\angle A + \\angle B + \\angle ACB = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Substitute the known values into the equation:\n\\[\n14^\\circ + \\angle B + 90^\\circ = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Simplify to solve for $\\angle B$:\n\\[\n104^\\circ + \\angle B = 180^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle B = 180^\\circ - 104^\\circ\n\\]\n\\[\n\\angle B = 76^\\circ\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\boxed{76}<|im_end|>",
